From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: S Ganesh <ganesh@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:54:30 -0700
Subject: Revoke Directory capability after unzip and harden extension unpack

Previously, Unzip() bound a self-owned storage::FilesystemImpl to serve
the storage::mojom::Directory capability passed to the unzipper utility
process. If the utility process retained that remote, it could continue
creating or overwriting files in the output directory after Unzip()
completed.

To prevent post-unzip tampering:
- UnzipOperation now owns a restricted Directory wrapper
  (UnzipFilesystemImpl) that enforces the path filter, create-only
  file opens, and single-delete of newly created files, and revokes the
  Directory receiver before running the completion callback (or on
  cancellation).
- SandboxedUnpacker::RewriteManifestFile and
  ComputedHashes::WriteToFile unlink existing files before writing so a
  retained file handle from the unzipper cannot modify them in place
  (matching sanitized images/message catalogs and indexed rulesets;
  verified_contents.json is signature-checked at use).
- CrxInstaller::ReloadExtensionAfterInstall verifies that the reloaded
  manifest matches the unpacked manifest (gated by
  kCrxInstallerVerifyReloadedManifest).

Bug: 574299586
Change-Id: Ibe2b286b85e1fba8a40320c19c93574b6ec01f25
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8594906
Reviewed-by: Takashi Toyoshima <toyoshim@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Andrea Orru <andreaorru@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: S Ganesh <ganesh@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1725153}
Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
extension_features.{h,cc}, enums.xml, crx_installer.h: the new feature,
histogram enum and ReloadManifestVerificationResult enum are inserted next
to the entries this branch has (the upstream neighbours do not exist
here). All functional hunks (crx_installer.cc, sandboxed_unpacker.cc,
computed_hashes.cc, unzip service) apply unchanged.
unzip.cc: the new UnzipFilesystemImpl does not override
Directory::GetDiskSpaceInfo()/ComputeDirectorySize(), which do not exist
in this branch's directory.mojom.

